    "abstract": "Illustrated parts breakdown of one upper deck seat track bay, showing the track sections, the attachment lugs, the splice hardware and the floor beam interface, with the pre and post modification alternates called out.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of one upper deck seat track bay and its attachment to the floor beam. Use it to order track sections, attachment lugs and splice hardware.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the bay looking down with the floor panels removed; sheet 2 shows the section through the track and the beam upper flange. The bay is symmetric about the aircraft centre line and only the left hand side is illustrated. The sealed track section at item 20 and its end caps at item 25 are not alternates of the open section: they carry a different splice pitch and a different lug seat, and item 20A, the open section, is shown only as the pre-modification cross reference so that a bay that has not been converted can still be ordered against. Item 10 and item 10A are the two attachment standards, the titanium lug on aircraft at the current standard and the earlier clip on aircraft that have not been converted. Do not mix standards within one bay. The figure was held and reissued once so that the bay is catalogued at the standard it will hold, rather than revised twice inside three years."
    },
